Now updates completely according how much time has passed", "channel": "C080X4GTZ0E", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1732588984.980229"}, {"ts": "1726880681.436589", "type": "message", "text": "So over the last couple of days, I played chapter 4 and 5 extensively, using Nate/Julius/Lexi. My overall feel is that:
1. A lot of levels didn't have enough pieces (low 20s)
2. Most levels are too easy (Win rate 90%+)
3. Several levels have not so great layouts where it's just multiple single stack pillars.
4. Some layouts are great for Domino Chest levels, some are not. Generally speaking, it seems like levels with multiple single stack pillars are not great for domino chest as the keys can often be buried underneath another key, where it's impossible to access.
5. I'm leaning towards [PERSON_NAME_4102]'s foresight revealing with a slight bias towards a key tile. (Not 100% priority, but like 50% chance of revealing a key tile, this probability is not disclosed to the player) Organically I was only able to have the "Fuck yeah!!!" moment when [PERSON_NAME_4102]'s foresight perfectly revealed a key tile that would otherwise been inaccessible due to it being a child of another key tile only ~15% of the time.
6. The reason for [PERSON_NAME_4102]'s success rate being low has to do with the layout, but more importantly, timing. Now that her foresight is 5 streak instead of 6 streak, she actually has a chance of revealing a key, where as she couldn't earlier. But even then the timing sometimes is too early, and she's revealing with a 1 in 10 face down tiles hoping for a key, and it usually ends up with failure. Things improve when There are like only 5 or less face down tiles left. Again I think a reveal bias probability will help
7. Bomb levels are usually still on the easy side, however I noticed that very often I finish a level without igniting all bombs. What this means is that players generally will still finish, but they just won't 3 star as easily because it's very often that they can't light all the fuses before having to be forced to match a bomb tile as a dud. This is good because [PERSON_NAME_1711] will definitely be the 3-star getter for these levels.
8. Some bomb levels have odd layouts where 3 bombs are all within range of each other and blowing up 1 of the bombs will just set off the other 2. These levels feel a bit meaningless.
9. [PERSON_NAME_1711] and [PERSON_NAME_7900]' removal can fuck up the flow by removing a bridge piece. I'm considering a bias as well in removing pieces that don't connect with other pieces on the board, or the tile in hand, or both. (50% chance it removes a piece with the stated condition here)
10. [PERSON_NAME_7900]' ability didn't seem to counter vanishing tile too much, because the timing of his removals aren't always perfect where a vanishing tile is facing up at the exact time his streak ability fires off. I might consider adding some ability to [PERSON_NAME_7900], and one of that is a "blizzard" spell (He's a wizard after all), and this blizzard spell will essentially "lock" a vanishing tile in ice, so it doesn't count down ever. Basically when this ability triggers, the players are playing the level with 1 less vanishing tile. I'm considering this to be his high level passive as well.
11. I get really excited about any levels with special tiles. Regular levels just feels a bit "boring" once you have tasted all the cool stuff and character abilities in action. I think this is good as the contrast really showcases the fun parts of the game.
12. Because of how easy the levels are, I can still breeze through it and pretty much 3-star with _any_ character and at level 1. This won't be good because we need to be demonstrating to players that character selection matters earlier in the game progression.", "channel": "C05H8KVNU67", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1726091369.828469", "type": "message", "text": "<!here> I want to take a moment to recognize and celebrate everything we’ve achieved together for our new build, Baklava! We are shipping it momentarily.

